1
00:00:06,291 --> 00:00:08,166
Oh, Delphee...

2
00:00:08,166 --> 00:00:10,958
hope someone's seen you.

3
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,166
<i>We are quite</i>
<i>proud of you, Ana.</i>

4
00:00:25,166 --> 00:00:28,375
I know we don't
say that much...

5
00:00:28,375 --> 00:00:29,250
Or ever.

6
00:00:29,250 --> 00:00:30,791
...but we see now

7
00:00:30,791 --> 00:00:33,458
that your... passion?
...for your studies

8
00:00:33,458 --> 00:00:36,791
was all in service of Imperium.

9
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:47,750
[Ana] A dragon! A real dragon!

10
00:00:47,750 --> 00:00:49,083
[grunting]

11
00:00:51,125 --> 00:00:52,791
[laughing]

12
00:00:52,791 --> 00:00:54,000
Aww.

13
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:55,666
You sweet thing.

14
00:00:55,666 --> 00:00:56,708
What's her name?

15
00:00:56,708 --> 00:00:59,333
Subject 152-9a,

16
00:00:59,333 --> 00:01:00,666
but some of the lab techs

17
00:01:00,666 --> 00:01:03,291
have taken
to calling her "Sora."

18
00:01:03,291 --> 00:01:04,625
Sora?

19
00:01:04,625 --> 00:01:07,458
The ancient Imperium
word for "orphan"?

20
00:01:07,458 --> 00:01:10,041
Did something happen
to your family, Sora?

21
00:01:13,166 --> 00:01:14,541
What are you doing?

22
00:01:14,541 --> 00:01:16,958
Demonstrating
the possibilities.

23
00:01:21,250 --> 00:01:22,083
[roaring]

24
00:01:22,083 --> 00:01:23,333
[Ana] What?! No!

25
00:01:23,333 --> 00:01:24,666
<i>No, stop!</i>

26
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:28,166
Waah!

27
00:01:35,958 --> 00:01:37,541
[horn honking]

28
00:01:37,541 --> 00:01:38,416
Unh!

29
00:01:45,958 --> 00:01:48,000
[gasping] My workbench!

30
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:50,375
If you won't use
your scientific studies

31
00:01:50,375 --> 00:01:52,291
to support Imperium...

32
00:01:52,291 --> 00:01:54,541
And all that we stand for...

33
00:01:54,541 --> 00:01:57,916
Then you'll just have
to find a new interest.

34
00:02:00,916 --> 00:02:02,041
[bicycle bell ringing]

35
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:10,416
I believed in you!

36
00:02:10,416 --> 00:02:13,208
I thought you were making
Imperium a better place!

37
00:02:13,208 --> 00:02:15,125
For every living thing!

38
00:02:17,291 --> 00:02:20,958
I know you wish I was a
dutiful Imperian, Mom and Dad,

39
00:02:20,958 --> 00:02:23,625
but I'll never be the daughter
you want me to be...

40
00:02:23,625 --> 00:02:26,375
that Empress Beatrix
wants me to be.

41
00:02:30,333 --> 00:02:32,250
[playing the flute]

42
00:02:39,083 --> 00:02:40,791
[rattling]

43
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:46,500
[screaming]

44
00:02:52,833 --> 00:02:54,458
[stomach rumbling]

45
00:02:54,458 --> 00:02:58,333
Urchin Fruit,
fresh from Merlopia.

46
00:03:00,166 --> 00:03:01,208
Uh-uh.

47
00:03:01,208 --> 00:03:03,416
Don't run a charity here, girl.

48
00:03:03,416 --> 00:03:05,250
No free food.

49
00:03:05,250 --> 00:03:07,625
And no foreign coin.

50
00:03:07,625 --> 00:03:10,375
The Crossroads
is still part of Ninjago.

51
00:03:10,375 --> 00:03:14,791
Hey, this price is triple
what you charged yesterday.

52
00:03:14,791 --> 00:03:19,291
How can you think about money
when people are hungry?

53
00:03:19,291 --> 00:03:23,875
A crisis for some
is an opportunity for others.

54
00:03:24,875 --> 00:03:28,041
[stomach rumbling]

55
00:03:31,916 --> 00:03:32,791
[gasping]

56
00:03:33,750 --> 00:03:34,625
Thief!

57
00:03:34,625 --> 00:03:35,625
[gasping]

58
00:03:35,625 --> 00:03:38,833
Well? Go after
that little pest!

59
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:42,583
Bah...

60
00:03:42,583 --> 00:03:46,666
Uh, fine, free fruit
to whoever catches her.

61
00:03:48,250 --> 00:03:49,916
[all muttering]

62
00:03:51,375 --> 00:03:52,250
[panting]

63
00:03:54,541 --> 00:03:55,458
[gasping]

64
00:03:58,166 --> 00:03:59,000
[gasping]

65
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:05,333
Whoa!

66
00:04:07,500 --> 00:04:08,625
Sorry about that.

67
00:04:08,625 --> 00:04:10,250
Hard to see
over all these pies.

68
00:04:11,166 --> 00:04:13,250
[man] I think she went
thattaway!

69
00:04:13,250 --> 00:04:14,250
[she gasps]

70
00:04:14,250 --> 00:04:16,541
Homemade pies. Plenty in stock.

71
00:04:16,541 --> 00:04:20,000
Ooh, all this chasin's
makin' me hungry.

72
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:20,958
I'll take this one.

73
00:04:20,958 --> 00:04:23,125
Uh, actually, all out of pies.

74
00:04:23,125 --> 00:04:25,000
We're closed.
Come back tomorrow.

75
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:28,041
I guess I could make myself
a mustard sandwich

76
00:04:28,041 --> 00:04:29,250
when I get home.

77
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:32,916
I think we're safe.

78
00:04:34,041 --> 00:04:35,625
[stomach grumbling]

79
00:04:35,625 --> 00:04:37,375
[Arin] You can have one
if you want.

80
00:04:37,375 --> 00:04:39,083
I baked them myself.

81
00:04:39,083 --> 00:04:40,500
[eating]

82
00:04:41,500 --> 00:04:42,625
[swallowing]

83
00:04:42,625 --> 00:04:44,000
[laughing]

84
00:04:45,333 --> 00:04:46,583
Thanks for helping me.

85
00:04:46,583 --> 00:04:48,041
Of course.

86
00:04:48,041 --> 00:04:50,333
The Merge brought everyone
together, right?

87
00:04:50,333 --> 00:04:54,291
So I believe together
is the only way to survive it.

88
00:04:54,291 --> 00:04:55,666
My name's Arin.

89
00:04:55,666 --> 00:04:57,416
I'm An--

90
00:04:58,416 --> 00:05:00,666
Uh, you can call me Sora.

91
00:05:04,333 --> 00:05:05,208
Sora?

92
00:05:05,208 --> 00:05:08,375
What are you all doing here?

93
00:05:10,583 --> 00:05:11,916
[Arin] Frak?

94
00:05:11,916 --> 00:05:13,791
[Ras snarling]

95
00:05:13,791 --> 00:05:16,500
Zane, you're...

96
00:05:16,500 --> 00:05:17,875
big.

97
00:05:20,416 --> 00:05:24,666
I guess a lot's changed
since we last saw each other.

98
00:05:25,625 --> 00:05:28,041
Arin, I...

99
00:05:28,041 --> 00:05:30,291
Ras, let him go!

100
00:05:30,291 --> 00:05:32,875
He is with me by choice.

101
00:05:32,875 --> 00:05:35,916
He's lying. Typical villain.

102
00:05:35,916 --> 00:05:38,250
No. It's true...

103
00:05:38,250 --> 00:05:40,583
Ras is my new teacher.

104
00:05:45,416 --> 00:05:48,750
♪ Lost in the unknown ♪

105
00:05:48,750 --> 00:05:51,625
♪ Together we will rise ♪

106
00:05:51,625 --> 00:05:55,083
♪ We fight ♪

107
00:05:55,083 --> 00:05:58,166
♪ Be a ninja
for what's right ♪

108
00:06:00,416 --> 00:06:02,666
[♪♪♪]

109
00:06:04,333 --> 00:06:06,458
Oh, hello.

110
00:06:06,458 --> 00:06:07,833
Let's see if you work.

111
00:06:10,250 --> 00:06:11,166
[clicking power button]

112
00:06:11,166 --> 00:06:13,541
[music playing in headphones]

113
00:06:13,541 --> 00:06:15,541
[laughing] Nice!

114
00:06:19,916 --> 00:06:21,916
[growling]

115
00:06:23,250 --> 00:06:24,708
[gasping]

116
00:06:24,708 --> 00:06:26,875
[barking]

117
00:06:26,875 --> 00:06:28,125
Unh!

118
00:06:28,125 --> 00:06:29,166
[barking]

119
00:06:29,166 --> 00:06:31,458
[turning music volume up]

120
00:06:31,458 --> 00:06:32,583
Wahoo!

121
00:06:34,166 --> 00:06:37,375
[music playing in headphones]

122
00:06:37,375 --> 00:06:39,333
[playing the flute]

123
00:06:56,166 --> 00:06:58,625
This Grapple Gun thing
you made me is amazing.

124
00:06:58,625 --> 00:06:59,708
[shooting]

125
00:07:03,416 --> 00:07:06,625
...or it will be
once I get the hang of it.

126
00:07:06,625 --> 00:07:09,500
You'll be a real Samurai
before you know it.

127
00:07:09,500 --> 00:07:10,958
Just like your heroes.

128
00:07:10,958 --> 00:07:13,958
Not samurai, Ninja.

129
00:07:13,958 --> 00:07:17,416
Masters of Spinjitsu. Ya! Ah!

130
00:07:17,416 --> 00:07:18,625
[Sora] Right, Ninja.

131
00:07:18,625 --> 00:07:21,458
Floyd, Kal, Lane, Mister Wu.

132
00:07:21,458 --> 00:07:24,750
No. Lloyd, Kai, Zane...

133
00:07:24,750 --> 00:07:26,708
[Sora laughing]

134
00:07:26,708 --> 00:07:28,250
You're teasing me.

135
00:07:28,250 --> 00:07:30,583
Only 'cause it's really fun.

136
00:07:30,583 --> 00:07:33,250
I mean, you carry that
green mask everywhere you go.

137
00:07:33,250 --> 00:07:36,041
We didn't have anything
like the Ninja where I'm from.

138
00:07:36,041 --> 00:07:37,958
Then how did you
tease your friends?

139
00:07:37,958 --> 00:07:40,500
I didn't have those either.

140
00:07:47,583 --> 00:07:49,500
About time
you had a proper oven.

141
00:07:49,500 --> 00:07:51,166
That campfire
you've been baking with

142
00:07:51,166 --> 00:07:52,541
is a fire hazard.

143
00:07:52,541 --> 00:07:55,541
[Arin] But it gave my pies
their rustic, crispy flavor.

144
00:07:55,541 --> 00:07:56,625
Aah!

145
00:07:56,625 --> 00:07:58,250
You mean burnt?

146
00:07:58,250 --> 00:08:00,250
Let's fire this baby up.

147
00:08:07,791 --> 00:08:09,333
[rattling]

148
00:08:10,083 --> 00:08:11,833
Aah!

149
00:08:11,833 --> 00:08:14,125
Ah! No, my recipes!

150
00:08:14,125 --> 00:08:15,916
I knew this was all a mistake!

151
00:08:15,916 --> 00:08:17,000
[gasping]

152
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:18,250
[sighing]

153
00:08:18,250 --> 00:08:21,458
Of course the Ninja's masks
would be flame-resistant.

154
00:08:21,458 --> 00:08:23,375
They'd have to be
with Kai around.

155
00:08:23,375 --> 00:08:25,875
Sora, you okay? Sorry I snapped.

156
00:08:25,875 --> 00:08:27,916
Sora?

157
00:08:31,500 --> 00:08:32,666
You heard the boy.

158
00:08:32,666 --> 00:08:35,375
My student will not
abandon his teacher.

159
00:08:35,375 --> 00:08:37,583
Ras must be brainwashing him.

160
00:08:37,583 --> 00:08:39,250
I'm training him.

161
00:08:39,250 --> 00:08:41,541
Like I was training you.

162
00:08:41,541 --> 00:08:43,625
Until I learned
who you really are!

163
00:08:43,625 --> 00:08:46,041
I don't need a reminder
of how evil Ras is.

164
00:08:46,041 --> 00:08:48,583
Nice people don't trap you
for eternity

165
00:08:48,583 --> 00:08:49,708
in the Nether-Space.

166
00:08:49,708 --> 00:08:51,750
[Lloyd] Enough!

167
00:08:51,750 --> 00:08:53,541
Arin, come back with us.

168
00:08:53,541 --> 00:08:55,500
We've been searching
everywhere for you.

169
00:08:55,500 --> 00:08:57,416
Technically, the search
that brought us here

170
00:08:57,416 --> 00:09:00,208
has been focused on finding
the remaining Prismatic Weapon

171
00:09:00,208 --> 00:09:02,041
that is currently
in the possession

172
00:09:02,041 --> 00:09:04,250
of our former ally, Arin.

173
00:09:04,250 --> 00:09:07,083
He's not our<i> former </i>ally.

174
00:09:07,083 --> 00:09:08,875
Do you have a blade
that looks like this?

175
00:09:08,875 --> 00:09:10,791
It's really important
we find it.

176
00:09:12,625 --> 00:09:15,083
Is this what you came for?

177
00:09:15,083 --> 00:09:18,666
Yes, this Returning Blade
is made of Prismatic Steel.

178
00:09:18,666 --> 00:09:20,375
I've had it for years...

179
00:09:20,375 --> 00:09:22,208
an old battle trophy.

180
00:09:22,208 --> 00:09:24,458
They're what the Forbidden
Five have been after.

181
00:09:24,458 --> 00:09:26,458
With the five Prismatic Weapons,

182
00:09:26,458 --> 00:09:27,708
they can release a Chaos Dragon

183
00:09:27,708 --> 00:09:30,375
that would throw the world
into, well, chaos.

184
00:09:30,375 --> 00:09:31,250
-[branch cracking]
-Look out!

185
00:09:31,666 --> 00:09:32,541
Aah!

186
00:09:35,291 --> 00:09:36,458
These two blades

187
00:09:36,458 --> 00:09:39,125
are the last ones the Five need
to free the dragon.

188
00:09:39,125 --> 00:09:42,833
Then I'll be sure to keep it
out of their hands.

189
00:09:42,833 --> 00:09:44,791
Arin, let us go.

190
00:09:46,500 --> 00:09:48,041
Arin, wait!

191
00:09:48,041 --> 00:09:50,708
You won't trick Arin
like you did me, Ras!

192
00:09:50,708 --> 00:09:51,583
Unh!

193
00:09:52,875 --> 00:09:53,750
[impact]

194
00:09:54,416 --> 00:09:55,333
Unh!

195
00:09:55,333 --> 00:09:57,333
[groaning]

196
00:09:57,333 --> 00:09:58,583
We don't want to fight you.

197
00:09:58,583 --> 00:10:00,625
Obviously. You're outnumbered.

198
00:10:00,625 --> 00:10:02,708
[sighing] Just let me go.

199
00:10:02,708 --> 00:10:04,583
I need Ras.

200
00:10:04,583 --> 00:10:06,291
Uh, Arin...

201
00:10:09,041 --> 00:10:11,458
Oh, come on!

202
00:10:16,250 --> 00:10:17,291
[laughing]

203
00:10:17,291 --> 00:10:20,541
Looks like we got
another stray.

204
00:10:20,541 --> 00:10:22,666
[chuckling]

205
00:10:22,666 --> 00:10:24,416
Sora, come back!

206
00:10:24,416 --> 00:10:26,500
There's hardly any burning!

207
00:10:27,166 --> 00:10:28,083
Have you seen Sora?

208
00:10:28,083 --> 00:10:30,375
She was just here.

209
00:10:30,375 --> 00:10:33,000
I think she went that way.

210
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:34,541
Ugh!

211
00:10:34,541 --> 00:10:36,916
Uh, thanks.

212
00:10:40,875 --> 00:10:44,500
Can't go back to Imperium,
but what else is out there?

213
00:10:44,500 --> 00:10:47,041
Gotta be somewhere I haven't
made a fool of myself

214
00:10:47,041 --> 00:10:49,375
and alienated
everyone I care about.

215
00:10:49,375 --> 00:10:50,333
[meowing]

216
00:10:51,500 --> 00:10:53,416
[meowing]

217
00:10:57,416 --> 00:10:59,500
Aw, poor thing.

218
00:10:59,500 --> 00:11:01,500
[purring]

219
00:11:01,500 --> 00:11:03,250
You must be lost.

220
00:11:03,250 --> 00:11:04,625
[meowing]

221
00:11:04,625 --> 00:11:05,791
Here, kitty.

222
00:11:05,791 --> 00:11:07,500
Ah!

223
00:11:07,500 --> 00:11:09,166
[Sora] I won't hurt you!

224
00:11:09,833 --> 00:11:12,250
Sora, wait up! I'm sorry!

225
00:11:12,250 --> 00:11:13,916
[meowing]

226
00:11:14,541 --> 00:11:16,750
[Sora] Don't be scared...

227
00:11:22,791 --> 00:11:24,291
[yowling]

228
00:11:24,291 --> 00:11:25,250
[door slamming]

229
00:11:26,250 --> 00:11:28,000
-[sighing]
-[cackling]

230
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:31,333
Another lonely Other-Realmer.

231
00:11:31,333 --> 00:11:32,625
You were right.

232
00:11:32,625 --> 00:11:34,666
The Crossroads
is a great source

233
00:11:34,666 --> 00:11:36,708
for workers for the mines.

234
00:11:36,708 --> 00:11:39,333
So many lost souls.

235
00:11:39,333 --> 00:11:40,916
[cackling]

236
00:11:42,708 --> 00:11:43,958
[engine starting]

237
00:11:43,958 --> 00:11:45,333
[struggling]

238
00:11:45,333 --> 00:11:46,208
Aah!

239
00:11:47,416 --> 00:11:48,375
Oh...

240
00:11:49,833 --> 00:11:50,750
[gasping]

241
00:11:50,750 --> 00:11:52,625
Hey! Where are you going?

242
00:11:52,625 --> 00:11:54,375
That's my best friend!

243
00:11:56,166 --> 00:11:58,708
[struggling]

244
00:11:58,708 --> 00:12:00,666
Who was that guy?

245
00:12:00,666 --> 00:12:03,666
My new least favorite person.

246
00:12:08,416 --> 00:12:10,416
I'm not losing Arin again.

247
00:12:16,625 --> 00:12:18,333
Come on!

248
00:12:21,666 --> 00:12:25,125
Since when is the World Forest
Ninjago's newest hot spot?

249
00:12:25,125 --> 00:12:27,333
They're here
for the Prismatic Blades.

250
00:12:27,333 --> 00:12:29,166
They'll have to go
through us first.

251
00:12:29,166 --> 00:12:31,000
Get that blade.

252
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:33,916
[hissing]

253
00:12:33,916 --> 00:12:37,708
Oh, this should be easy.

254
00:12:37,708 --> 00:12:40,583
You're gonna regret
sending your little army away.

255
00:12:40,583 --> 00:12:43,166
Am I?

256
00:12:46,041 --> 00:12:47,541
Release me at once,

257
00:12:47,541 --> 00:12:49,916
or you'll face
an eternity of retribution!

258
00:13:06,500 --> 00:13:07,708
I see him!

259
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:10,833
Behind you!

260
00:13:11,541 --> 00:13:12,416
Unh!

261
00:13:12,416 --> 00:13:13,791
Aah!

262
00:13:15,208 --> 00:13:16,666
[screeching]

263
00:13:16,666 --> 00:13:17,625
[roaring]

264
00:13:18,500 --> 00:13:19,416
Aah!

265
00:13:23,666 --> 00:13:25,208
[Arin] Let him go!

266
00:13:29,125 --> 00:13:29,958
Haah!

267
00:13:29,958 --> 00:13:30,833
Yaah!

268
00:13:30,833 --> 00:13:32,000
-[grunting]
-[snarling]

269
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:33,166
Yaah!

270
00:13:33,166 --> 00:13:34,000
Unh!

271
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:35,416
Aah!

272
00:13:36,750 --> 00:13:38,458
[gasping]

273
00:13:39,708 --> 00:13:40,916
Aah!

274
00:13:40,916 --> 00:13:41,875
[grunting]

275
00:13:48,125 --> 00:13:49,833
Lloyd, get out of here
with the Blade.

276
00:13:49,833 --> 00:13:51,541
Let us handle him.

277
00:13:52,541 --> 00:13:56,250
Any thoughts on fighting
against Rising Dragon technique?

278
00:13:59,291 --> 00:14:00,750
Yaar!

279
00:14:02,083 --> 00:14:04,416
Huh? Where did he go?

280
00:14:04,416 --> 00:14:05,500
Aah!

281
00:14:05,500 --> 00:14:08,208
Time to blast this guy
back to the Nether-Space.

282
00:14:08,208 --> 00:14:09,083
Yaah!

283
00:14:11,250 --> 00:14:13,375
Uh... is this guy bugs?

284
00:14:13,375 --> 00:14:15,375
Is this guy bugs?!

285
00:14:15,375 --> 00:14:17,666
Yaah! Aw, that's
worse than puppets.

286
00:14:17,666 --> 00:14:19,791
[cackling]

287
00:14:20,791 --> 00:14:22,500
[struggling]

288
00:14:22,500 --> 00:14:23,708
[Nya] There's too many of them.

289
00:14:25,500 --> 00:14:26,583
[klaxon sounding]

290
00:14:26,583 --> 00:14:29,333
Prepare for
a premature landing.

291
00:14:31,166 --> 00:14:32,458
Do you mean "crash"?

292
00:14:34,916 --> 00:14:35,916
Aah!

293
00:14:38,666 --> 00:14:40,500
What good
is a legendary weapon

294
00:14:40,500 --> 00:14:42,000
if I'm not going to use it?

295
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:43,416
Aah!

296
00:14:45,041 --> 00:14:46,083
Huh?

297
00:14:49,500 --> 00:14:50,625
[gasping]

298
00:14:59,083 --> 00:15:00,541
Thank you.

299
00:15:00,541 --> 00:15:01,791
Aah! Unh!

300
00:15:01,791 --> 00:15:03,458
[struggling]

301
00:15:07,125 --> 00:15:08,583
Yaah!

302
00:15:10,041 --> 00:15:10,958
Aah!

303
00:15:10,958 --> 00:15:11,916
[grunting]

304
00:15:11,916 --> 00:15:13,541
[Nya screaming]

305
00:15:14,333 --> 00:15:15,541
[struggling]

306
00:15:15,541 --> 00:15:17,000
Aah! Hah!

307
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:18,541
Huh...

308
00:15:18,541 --> 00:15:20,208
[gasping]

309
00:15:20,958 --> 00:15:21,958
[grunting]

310
00:15:21,958 --> 00:15:23,916
That didn't work out
like I hoped.

311
00:15:25,625 --> 00:15:26,500
[blade slicing]

312
00:15:26,500 --> 00:15:27,750
[sighing]

313
00:15:29,541 --> 00:15:33,041
Let me outta here,
you numbskulls!

314
00:15:34,916 --> 00:15:36,458
[sighing]

315
00:15:37,708 --> 00:15:39,291
[Arin panting]

316
00:15:39,291 --> 00:15:40,583
Hold on, Sora!

317
00:15:40,583 --> 00:15:41,500
[panting]

318
00:15:42,500 --> 00:15:43,666
Think Ninja, Arin.

319
00:15:43,666 --> 00:15:46,166
There's more than one way
to catch a villain.

320
00:15:46,166 --> 00:15:50,083
They have speed,
but I know shortcuts.

321
00:15:52,083 --> 00:15:53,333
Coming through!

322
00:15:55,375 --> 00:15:56,875
Sorry, sorry.

323
00:15:58,625 --> 00:16:01,000
Hmm. These Ooze Berries
would be great in a pie.

324
00:16:01,750 --> 00:16:03,208
Huh! Yaah!

325
00:16:05,958 --> 00:16:07,250
Aah!

326
00:16:10,583 --> 00:16:12,375
Here goes nothing.

327
00:16:12,375 --> 00:16:14,083
[brakes screeching]

328
00:16:14,083 --> 00:16:15,750
Ninja...

329
00:16:15,750 --> 00:16:16,750
now!

330
00:16:27,041 --> 00:16:29,166
[Skulkin] These crossroad
roads are so confusing.

331
00:16:29,166 --> 00:16:30,041
[impact]

332
00:16:30,041 --> 00:16:31,000
[landing]

333
00:16:38,041 --> 00:16:39,250
[meowing]

334
00:16:41,833 --> 00:16:44,833
It's okay, I forgive you.

335
00:16:44,833 --> 00:16:46,625
I know what it's like
to be used

336
00:16:46,625 --> 00:16:48,416
and to hurt people
without knowing better.

337
00:16:48,416 --> 00:16:49,750
[yowling and scratching]

338
00:16:49,750 --> 00:16:51,500
Ow! Ugh!

339
00:16:51,500 --> 00:16:53,041
So much for being nice.

340
00:16:54,333 --> 00:16:55,541
Huh!

341
00:16:55,541 --> 00:16:56,375
Sora!

342
00:16:56,375 --> 00:16:57,541
I'm here to save you.

343
00:16:57,541 --> 00:16:58,541
[cat yowling]

344
00:16:58,541 --> 00:16:59,666
[hissing]

345
00:16:59,666 --> 00:17:00,666
Really?

346
00:17:00,666 --> 00:17:02,291
You said
this was all a mistake.

347
00:17:02,291 --> 00:17:04,375
I thought you didn't want
to be friends anymore.

348
00:17:04,375 --> 00:17:05,958
What?! No way!

349
00:17:05,958 --> 00:17:09,916
Friends make mistakes
all the time. That's normal.

350
00:17:09,916 --> 00:17:13,166
You really haven't had
any friends before, have you?

351
00:17:17,083 --> 00:17:18,208
Come on.

352
00:17:18,208 --> 00:17:22,000
I told you, the only way
through this is together.

353
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:23,833
I said, take a left!

354
00:17:23,833 --> 00:17:25,916
A left! Yaah!

355
00:17:25,916 --> 00:17:27,041
Whaa!

356
00:17:27,041 --> 00:17:28,000
[Sora gasping]

357
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:29,333
[meowing]

358
00:17:34,125 --> 00:17:37,250
I've never been so glad
to see that green mask.

359
00:17:37,250 --> 00:17:40,125
So, you think
I look like a Ninja?

360
00:17:40,125 --> 00:17:40,958
-Look out!
-Whoa!

361
00:17:40,958 --> 00:17:42,625
Hey! This isn't a bus.

362
00:17:42,625 --> 00:17:44,458
Get back in your cage.

363
00:17:44,458 --> 00:17:46,250
Hold on tight.

364
00:17:46,250 --> 00:17:47,708
You sure
you can work that thing?

365
00:17:47,708 --> 00:17:50,375
I hope so. It was built
by a genius.

366
00:17:54,125 --> 00:17:55,000
[screaming]

367
00:17:57,041 --> 00:17:58,208
[screaming]

368
00:17:58,208 --> 00:17:59,208
[yowling]

369
00:17:59,208 --> 00:18:00,208
[Skulkin shouting]

370
00:18:02,666 --> 00:18:04,000
[roaring]

371
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:05,833
Aah!

372
00:18:05,833 --> 00:18:07,000
Unh!

373
00:18:08,083 --> 00:18:09,708
Ugh!

374
00:18:09,708 --> 00:18:11,583
Thanks, just what I needed.

375
00:18:18,125 --> 00:18:19,083
Unh!

376
00:18:19,083 --> 00:18:20,916
What took you so long?

377
00:18:20,916 --> 00:18:22,250
I guess I shouldn't expect

378
00:18:22,250 --> 00:18:24,000
to learn gratitude
from you, huh?

379
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:24,833
Hurry!

380
00:18:24,833 --> 00:18:26,000
[cutting rope]

381
00:18:27,833 --> 00:18:29,416
[crying out]

382
00:18:32,041 --> 00:18:33,291
[rope tightening]

383
00:18:33,833 --> 00:18:34,708
Unh!

384
00:18:34,708 --> 00:18:35,583
Haah!

385
00:18:37,041 --> 00:18:38,791
[panting]

386
00:18:38,791 --> 00:18:41,208
This fool has become
more of an obstacle

387
00:18:41,208 --> 00:18:43,125
than your former Ninja allies.

388
00:18:43,125 --> 00:18:44,500
[Arin] They're not my former...

389
00:18:44,500 --> 00:18:45,375
Get down!

390
00:18:46,750 --> 00:18:47,708
Unh!

391
00:18:47,708 --> 00:18:48,583
[impact]

392
00:18:51,625 --> 00:18:52,500
[blow landing]

393
00:18:52,500 --> 00:18:53,875
[grunting]

394
00:18:55,416 --> 00:18:56,583
[snarling]

395
00:19:01,791 --> 00:19:02,875
Aah!

396
00:19:19,166 --> 00:19:20,333
Whaa...

397
00:19:20,333 --> 00:19:21,291
Arin!

398
00:19:21,291 --> 00:19:23,208
Yaah!

399
00:19:27,625 --> 00:19:29,041
[gasping]

400
00:19:29,041 --> 00:19:30,041
No!

401
00:19:38,083 --> 00:19:39,666
Whaa!

402
00:19:41,708 --> 00:19:42,833
[Sora sniffing]

403
00:19:42,833 --> 00:19:46,583
Ah, those Ooze Berries
smell amazing!

404
00:19:50,791 --> 00:19:53,083
[Arin crying out]

405
00:19:54,791 --> 00:19:57,083
[Sora] This could be
your best pie yet.

406
00:19:57,083 --> 00:19:59,291
You sure you don't miss
the special burnt crust

407
00:19:59,291 --> 00:20:00,458
my campfire made?

408
00:20:00,458 --> 00:20:03,625
[both laughing]

409
00:20:06,083 --> 00:20:08,416
Stronger together, right?

410
00:20:10,833 --> 00:20:12,333
Together forever.

411
00:20:15,875 --> 00:20:16,708
Hold on!

412
00:20:20,916 --> 00:20:22,083
Take my hand!

413
00:20:23,041 --> 00:20:24,416
[Arin] I got you!

414
00:20:25,083 --> 00:20:26,708
-Thanks for saving me.
-I'm sorry.

415
00:20:32,875 --> 00:20:35,500
Come back with us.
It won't be like before.

416
00:20:35,500 --> 00:20:37,291
We can find your parents.

417
00:20:39,416 --> 00:20:42,083
I already found my parents.

418
00:20:42,083 --> 00:20:43,541
They're dead.

419
00:20:58,416 --> 00:20:59,291
[blow landing]

420
00:21:00,166 --> 00:21:01,250
[roaring]

421
00:21:04,708 --> 00:21:05,916
[crying out]

422
00:21:06,916 --> 00:21:08,125
[grunting]

423
00:21:08,125 --> 00:21:09,625
[snarling]

424
00:21:18,208 --> 00:21:19,083
[squawking]

425
00:21:27,916 --> 00:21:30,041
[growling]

426
00:21:32,500 --> 00:21:34,791
They have all the Blades.

427
00:21:34,791 --> 00:21:36,791
Now there is nothing
to stop them

428
00:21:36,791 --> 00:21:39,416
from unleashing
the Chaos Dragon.

429
00:21:39,416 --> 00:21:41,166
[crying out]

430
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:46,791
[♪♪♪]

